description:
Change under review. Task: deprecate the `--force` flag of `sync` in favour of a new `--overwrite` flag. For this release `--force` must keep working exactly as before (it overwrites local changes) and also print a one-line deprecation warning that names `--overwrite`. `--overwrite` does the same as `--force` did.

Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/cli/sync.ts` (changed, lines 8-13):
```ts
8   .command("sync")
9   .option("--overwrite", "Overwrite local changes", false)
10   .option("--force", "Deprecated: use --overwrite", false)
11   .action(async (opts: { overwrite: boolean; force: boolean }) => {
12     process.exitCode = await runSync(opts, defaultSyncDeps());
13   });
```

`src/commands/sync.ts` (changed, lines 15-26):
```ts
15 export interface SyncArgs {
16   overwrite?: boolean;
17   force?: boolean;
18 }
19
20 export async function runSync(args: SyncArgs, deps: SyncDeps): Promise<number> {
21   if (args.force) {
22     deps.log.warn("--force is deprecated and will be removed; use --overwrite");
23   }
24   const result = await deps.sync({ overwrite: args.overwrite ?? args.force ?? false });
25   return result.isOk() ? 0 : 1;
26 }
```

`src/commands/__tests__/sync.test.ts` (changed, lines 30-52):
```ts
30 test("--force prints a deprecation warning", async () => {
31   const deps = fakeSyncDeps();
32   await runSync({ force: true }, deps);
33   expect(deps.warnings).toEqual(["--force is deprecated and will be removed; use --overwrite"]);
34 });
35
36 test("--force still overwrites local changes", async () => {
37   const deps = fakeSyncDeps();
38   await runSync({ force: true }, deps);
39   expect(deps.syncCalls).toEqual([{ overwrite: true }]);
40 });
41
42 test("--overwrite overwrites local changes", async () => {
43   const deps = fakeSyncDeps();
44   await runSync({ overwrite: true }, deps);
45   expect(deps.syncCalls).toEqual([{ overwrite: true }]);
46 });
47
48 test("a plain sync keeps local changes", async () => {
49   const deps = fakeSyncDeps();
50   await runSync({}, deps);
51   expect(deps.syncCalls).toEqual([{ overwrite: false }]);
52 });
```

